{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug RCA and pre-Gerrit repair report.\n\nProblem: the bridge cadence proof consumed 100.66-130.59s in every Ubuntu matrix cell, despite asserting one immutable workflow schedule.\n\nProven root cause: tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_push_policy.py called _bridge_schedule() inside the 24*60 minute scan. Each call reparsed reconcile-bridge.yml, so one invariant was loaded 1,440 times. Runtime counting observed the repeated boundary executing; hoisting only that acquisition collapsed the same exhaustive proof from a 8.75s local median (14.12/8.30/8.75s) to 0.59s (0.60/0.59/0.57s), rejecting cron matching itself as the dominant cost. The explicit CI performance requirement and test contract classify this as a defect. No caller behavior depends on repeated parsing.\n\nRED/GREEN: a focused boundary-count oracle in test_bridge_backstop_fires_on_a_uniform_hourly_cadence failed before the repair because parses exceeded one. It was physically held out from the fixer. The fixer hoisted schedule = _bridge_schedule() above the comprehension while retaining all 1,440 minute evaluations, the exact 24 fires, and the circular 60-minute gap proof. The held-out oracle then passed. Reintroducing _bridge_schedule() inside the loop returned it to RED; restoring the hoist returned it to GREEN. The observable assertion is boundary invocation count plus unchanged cadence results, so behavior-preserving refactors remain green.\n\nReplication and safety: focused file 37 passed; make lint and make typecheck passed from the worktree venv; pre-commit repeated lint/typecheck successfully. Same-host wall time fell 8.16s / 93.3% locally without reducing assertions, platform cells, or coverage. No production code, dependency, external effect, or test weakening is involved. Construct sweep found no other repeated _bridge_schedule call in this proof; no parity surfaces apply to a test-local helper. Residual risk: the separate test-wide YAML/AST/Pandoc repeated-boundary patterns remain tracked on linked remediation tickets, not hidden in this fix. Commit 4c4225c3dd is ready for Gerrit once the existing unrelated CI run completes."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786673254867079001,"uuid":"60cdc307-b113-48bc-b24a-885f9895b618"}